What:		/sys/bus/counter/devices/counterX/countY/alarm_value
KernelVersion:	6.18
Contact:	Espressif Linux Port Maintainers <linux-riscv@espressif.com>
Description:
		Compare value for an ESP32-P4 timer-group alarm, in counter
		ticks. Write a value from 0 through 2^54 - 1 with the alarm
		disarmed. A write to an armed alarm returns -EBUSY.

What:		/sys/bus/counter/devices/counterX/countY/alarm_enable
KernelVersion:	6.18
Contact:	Espressif Linux Port Maintainers <linux-riscv@espressif.com>
Description:
		Write 1 to arm the compare event, or 0 to disarm it.
		A match produces COUNTER_EVENT_THRESHOLD on channel Y.
		In one-shot mode the alarm then disarms while the timer can
		continue counting. Stopping the counter disarms its alarm.

What:		/sys/bus/counter/devices/counterX/countY/autoreload
KernelVersion:	6.18
Contact:	Espressif Linux Port Maintainers <linux-riscv@espressif.com>
Description:
		Write 1 for periodic alarms or 0 for one-shot alarms. In
		periodic mode a compare match reloads the value last written
		to countY/count. The interrupt handler rearms the alarm.
		If the requested period is shorter than the time needed to
		service the interrupt, compare events can be missed.
